      {
        "id": 87651,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-15T03:00:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I just finished a really tense game of BIIIIIIIIIRDS IIIIIIIIIN SPAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACE, where I played with all the Vengeance heroes. It was something I tried back in playtesting, but back then the heroes were far from their best (*coughSETBACKcough*) so I died miserably. I decided to give it a second go around, and this time -- apart from KNYFE and Setback, who died early before I got my tanking/healing racket that is the Sentinels properly established -- everyone survived with full health. The Matriarch ended up flipping no less than 5 times, helped along a bit by Parse using Updated Intel to push all the birds to the top and discard all the really bad stuff. I almost had to deal with the cohorts a second time, but a well-planned Buffer Overflow took care of that problem before it even started. She ended up going down to 40, healing back up to full, and THEN being pummelled down while on her Ruler of the Flock side. I could have killed her earlier in the round, but instead I decided to go for the more thematic kill and first cleared the mask, carrion fields, and all 12 birds in play from the board before reducing her to 1 HP and insta-killing her with Cornered Beast.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:12:00.027Z",
