      {
        "id": 87652,
        "name": "bessyrocks12",
        "username": "bessyrocks12",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bessyrocks12/{size}/2447_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-17T05:14:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We had a rather dramatic game last week. Three hour game utilizing 3 Vengance characters (plus one homebrew) seemed to be absolutely in hand (you know, for a terribly long game). It had been drawn out by lots of getting used to the decks and the villain strategies. Ermine seemed to keep herself redirecting attacks all game while Blade stayed buffed. We seemingly couldn't get any of the ongoing destruction that we needed, and our ongoings were constantly being pulled out of the game. I was using the Sentinels and using Medico to keep everyone healthy until I started Blocking with Mainstay. We had taken down Friction and Fright Train, but Setback and Parse were running low. Freedom Tower was keeping highest and lowest +1 and -1 respectively, but Blade was abusing us even when we finally incapped him. It came down to Ermine and the mini-nemises, but Setback had taken far too much hurt, the Sentinels couldn't keep rolling, and KNYFE and the homebrew fizzled. An Entry Point mixed with the +1 already in play from the environment was dealing serious damage from the villains. Coming from being down, getting back in with some epic Setback and Sentinels, but eventually collapsing made for a roller coaster game.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
